<div class="programme">
  <h2><a href="https://tickets.phoenix.org.uk/PhoenixCinemaLeicester.dll/TSelectItems.waSelectItemsPrompt.TcsWebMenuItem_437.TcsWebTab_438.TcsProgramme_13939137">The Lost Children of Tuam</a> (12A)</h2>
  <div class="fivecol">
    <div class="image">
      <img src="https://images.savoysystems.co.uk/PHL/13992252.jpg"/>
    </div>
	<div class="synopsis"><p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733; &#8211; Guardian. A local historian embarks on a painstaking investigation in Country Galway that brings her into conflict with the Church, State, and local town.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733; &#8211; Guardian</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;"><br /></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733; &#8211; Times</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;"><br /></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">Based on The New York Times article of the same name by Dan Berry,</span><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: bold; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">&nbsp;The Lost Children of Tuam</span><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">&nbsp;follows the true story of history enthusiast Catherine Corless (Monica Dolan) who uncovered a devastating truth while researching the Bon Secours Mother and Baby Home in Tuam, County Galway. As she embarks on a painstaking investigation Catherine faces opposition from the Church, the State, and even her hometown.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;"><br /></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px; margin: 0px 0px 0px 0px;"><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">A powerful and moving dramatisation of a shocking and appalling true story from Ireland&#8217;s past. Acclaimed Irish filmmaker Frank Berry (</span><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: bold; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">Michael Inside, Aisha</span><span style=" ignore-font-size: 10pt; ignore-font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; ignore-color: #000000; background-color: transparent; text-decoration: none;">) directs.</span></p>
</div>
  </div>
